Package: dmemcg-booster
Architecture: linux-any
Depends: systemd, ${misc:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}
Recommends: sparky-stereo-vram-boost
XB-Bugs: https://github.com/Sparky-OS/sparky-stereo-os/issues
Description: enable the dmem cgroup controller so the foreground game keeps its VRAM
 Linux 7.3 lets a cgroup's dmem.min and dmem.low protect its video memory
 when other programs push it out of VRAM, on drivers that register their
 VRAM with the dmem cgroup controller (amdgpu, xe and nouveau).
 This service turns that controller on in the cgroups systemd creates,
 at system level and in each user's session, and gives the user's
 applications (app.slice) the GPUs' whole VRAM as their protection, so a
 desktop program in the background loses VRAM before the game in front.
 A foreground booster such as plasma-foreground-booster then gives the
 window in front the protection.
 .
 This is Natalie Vock's dmemcg-booster 0.1.3 (Valve Corporation, MIT),
 from https://gitlab.steamos.cloud/holo/dmemcg-booster, built with
 Debian's Rust crates. The edition starts it only where
 sparky-stereo-vram-boost finds an AMD GPU with its own VRAM.
